"use strict";(self.webpackChunkknowledge_graph_plugin=self.webpackChunkknowledge_graph_plugin||[]).push([[6285],{19192(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"/2026/05/05/site-restructure-v2","metadata":{"permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/05/05/site-restructure-v2","source":"@site/docs-updates/2026-05-05-site-restructure-v2.mdx","title":"Docs restructured around five user skill pillars","description":"The KMGraph documentation site has been reorganized from a flat guides taxonomy into five skill-based pillars. Navigation now mirrors what users are actually trying to do.","date":"2026-05-05T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Docs restructured around five user skill pillars"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Home page redesigned - clearer audience, context grid, demo GIF","permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/04/09/homepage-rewrite"}},"content":"The KMGraph documentation site has been reorganized from a flat guides taxonomy into five skill-based pillars. Navigation now mirrors what users are actually trying to do.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Why the change\\n\\nThe previous structure organized content by feature area \u2014 Guides, Reference, Concepts. This forced users to know what KMGraph calls things before they could find what they needed. Someone who just fixed a bug and wants to save it had to navigate to \\"Guides\\" \u2192 \\"Lesson Capture\\" rather than finding a section that just says \\"I solved something.\\"\\n\\nThe new structure is organized around five questions users actually ask themselves.\\n\\n## Five pillars\\n\\nEach pillar is a top-level sidebar section with a one-line user question:\\n\\n| Pillar | Question |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Capturing** | I solved something. How do I save it? |\\n| **Recalling** | I think I\'ve solved this before. |\\n| **Organizing** | How do I keep this from becoming a junk drawer? |\\n| **Portability** | I use multiple AI tools. Make them share knowledge. |\\n| **Tailoring** | I want this to fit my workflow. |\\n\\n## Landing page\\n\\nThe home page now leads with a pillar card grid immediately after the install hero \u2014 five clickable cards, each with its user question, so first-time visitors can self-route to the right section without reading the full docs.\\n\\n## Content changes\\n\\n- All guides moved from `docs/guides/` into the appropriate pillar\\n- `META-ISSUE-GUIDE.md` and `PATTERNS-GUIDE.md` merged into the Capturing pillar pages\\n- `WORKFLOWS.md` archive/restore content merged into Recalling \u2192 Session Memory\\n- `me-and-rules.mdx` split: AI profile \u2192 Portability; session memory \u2192 Recalling\\n- `4-PILLARS.md` and `4-LAYERS.md` moved to `docs/concepts/` as proper concept pages\\n- `COMMAND-GUIDE.md` moved to `docs/reference/command-guide.md`\\n- `CONCEPTS.md` decomposed into four focused concept pages\\n- `capture-from-bugfix.md` merged into `capture-lessons-learned.md` \u2014 one canonical capture page\\n\\n## Page structure alignment\\n\\nAll 24 pillar pages were aligned to a consistent internal structure:\\n\\n- Blockquote framing question immediately after H1\\n- `## Goal`, `## Prerequisites`, `## Steps`, `## Verify` boilerplate removed \u2014 content folded into conceptual H2s\\n- Heavy reference material moved to `## Reference` appendices (after `---`)\\n- `## Related` last on every page, with descriptive em-dash link labels\\n- `search-the-graph.md` rewritten from a prose essay to a structured H2 page\\n\\n## What didn\'t change\\n\\nCommand syntax, MCP tools, plugin behavior \u2014 none of that changed. This is a navigation and organization update only."},{"id":"/2026/04/09/homepage-rewrite","metadata":{"permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/04/09/homepage-rewrite","source":"@site/docs-updates/2026-04-09-homepage-rewrite.mdx","title":"Home page redesigned - clearer audience, context grid, demo GIF","description":"The KMGraph home page has been redesigned based on user feedback. The previous page didn\'t immediately answer who KMGraph is for or what it does - visitors had to read too far before the value was clear.","date":"2026-04-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Home page redesigned - clearer audience, context grid, demo GIF"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Docs restructured around five user skill pillars","permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/05/05/site-restructure-v2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Documentation restructured \u2014 Di\xe1taxis IA, search, demos","permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/04/08/docusaurus-restructure"}},"content":"The KMGraph home page has been redesigned based on user feedback. The previous page didn\'t immediately answer who KMGraph is for or what it does - visitors had to read too far before the value was clear.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**New banner** - updated to lead with the audience hook, the problem, and the solution in a single visual:\\n- *\\"Using an AI coding assistant? KMGraph is for you.\\"*\\n- *\\"KMGraph remembers what you and your tools forget.\\"*\\n- *\\"Lessons Learned. Decisions. Institutional Knowledge.\\"*\\n\\n**Context grid** - a 2\xd72 grid immediately answers \\"what does it bridge?\\": sessions, models, tools, and teammates.\\n\\n**What it stores** - three plain-language bullets mapping directly to the tricolon: lessons learned, decisions, and institutional knowledge.\\n\\n**Audience badges** - explicit audience callout: Developer \xb7 Vibe-Coder \xb7 Prompt Engineer \xb7 Open-Source Maintainer \xb7 Small Agile Team.\\n\\n**Demo GIF** - `capture-lesson` demo now shown on the home page so visitors see the tool in action before being asked to install it."},{"id":"/2026/04/08/docusaurus-restructure","metadata":{"permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/04/08/docusaurus-restructure","source":"@site/docs-updates/2026-04-08-docusaurus-restructure.mdx","title":"Documentation restructured \u2014 Di\xe1taxis IA, search, demos","description":"The KMGraph documentation site has been fully restructured using the Di\xe1taxis information architecture: Tutorials, How-to Guides, Reference, and Concepts. Every page now has a clear intent, and navigation reflects what you\'re trying to do \u2014 not internal feature groupings.","date":"2026-04-08T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Documentation restructured \u2014 Di\xe1taxis IA, search, demos"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Home page redesigned - clearer audience, context grid, demo GIF","permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/04/09/homepage-rewrite"},"nextItem":{"title":"Homepage visuals, UX improvements, and doc fixes","permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/github-docs-visuals"}},"content":"The KMGraph documentation site has been fully restructured using the [Di\xe1taxis](https://diataxis.fr) information architecture: Tutorials, How-to Guides, Reference, and Concepts. Every page now has a clear intent, and navigation reflects what you\'re trying to do \u2014 not internal feature groupings.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n**New structure**\\n\\n- **Quickstart** \u2014 zero-to-first-lesson in 5 minutes with terminal demo GIFs\\n- **15 how-to guides** \u2014 task-oriented recipes: capture from a bugfix, write a pattern, sync across machines, integrate with Obsidian/Notion/NotebookLM, and more\\n- **Reference** \u2014 commands, skills, agents, hooks, and templates in sortable tables; condensed from the old COMMAND-GUIDE\\n- **Concepts** \u2014 explanatory pages for the mental models behind KMGraph (why it exists, the four pillars, personal vs project KGs, the automation layer)\\n\\n**Demo GIFs**\\n\\nEvery core command now has a VHS terminal recording embedded in the Quickstart page: `init`, `status`, `recall`, `capture-lesson`, and `session-summary`.\\n\\n**Search**\\n\\nFull-text search is active via `@orama/plugin-docusaurus-v3` \u2014 no crawler required.\\n\\n**Glossary tooltips**\\n\\nKMGraph-specific terms (lesson, ADR, KG, skill, agent, capture, recall, session, handoff, hook, pattern) now show definition tooltips on hover via the new `<Glossary>` component.\\n\\n## Files removed\\n\\nThe following legacy pages were split into the new structure and removed:\\n\\n- `GETTING-STARTED.md` \u2192 Quickstart + Troubleshooting + reference/agents + reference/skills\\n- `CHANGELOG-DOCS-ONLY.md` \u2192 seeded into this `docs-updates/` feed\\n- `_test-layout.md`, `DEPLOYMENT-SITEMAP.md`, `NAVIGATION-INDEX.md` \u2014 orphaned, removed"},{"id":"github-docs-visuals","metadata":{"permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/github-docs-visuals","source":"@site/docs-updates/2026-02-26-github-docs-visuals.mdx","title":"Homepage visuals, UX improvements, and doc fixes","description":"Initial documentation site improvements: homepage journey flow diagram, expanded scenarios, and accessibility fixes.","date":"2026-02-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"slug":"github-docs-visuals","title":"Homepage visuals, UX improvements, and doc fixes"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Documentation restructured \u2014 Di\xe1taxis IA, search, demos","permalink":"/knowledge-graph/docs-updates/2026/04/08/docusaurus-restructure"}},"content":"Initial documentation site improvements: homepage journey flow diagram, expanded scenarios, and accessibility fixes.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Homepage Visuals & UX\\n\\n- **Journey Flow Mermaid Diagram**: Replaced bulleted scenarios with a narrative left-to-right flow.\\n- **Expanded Scenarios**: Added trigger moments and future payoffs (including agile sprint retrospectives).\\n- **\\"About This Project\\" Repositioning**: Moved project backstory to the bottom of the page in a collapsed info box.\\n- **\\"How It Works\\" Concrete Rewrite**: Clarified markdown-based storage and absence of external database dependencies.\\n- **Feature Discoverability**: Set the full feature list to be open by default.\\n- **Intro Sentence**: Added a guiding sentence before the journey flow diagram.\\n- **Typography**: Removed emdashes from descriptive text for a cleaner documentation style.\\n\\n## General Documentation Updates\\n\\n- **Universal Installer Clarification**: Added details to `GETTING-STARTED.md` regarding behavioral expectations and terminal/file access requirements.\\n- **Fragment Links & Anchors**: Fixed broken internal navigation links in `COMMAND-GUIDE.md` and `NAVIGATION-INDEX.md`.\\n- **Accessibility Fixes**: Added `accTitle` and `accDescr` to all new diagrams for Section 508 compliance.\\n- **Typo Fix**: Corrected missing space in `index.md` Outcome card."}]}}')}}]);